NAME
       lseek - reposition a file offset

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       off_t lseek(int fd, off_t offset, int whence);

DESCRIPTION
       Moves the file offset of FD.

       SEEK_SET   offset from the start
       SEEK_CUR   offset from the current position
       SEEK_END   offset from the end

RETURN VALUE
       The new offset, or -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EBADF    fd is not open
       EINVAL   whence is not one of the three, or the result would be
                negative
       ESPIPE   fd refers to a pipe or a terminal

SEE ALSO
       open(2), read(2), write(2), truncate(2)
